-- chem/hubbard.cub — local lower certificates for electrons: the Hubbard chain at half filling, in the particle–hole
-- symmetric form H = −Σ_{i,σ} (c†_{iσ} c_{i+1σ} + h.c.) + U Σ_i (n_{i↑} − ½)(n_{i↓} − ½). A k-site open patch H_k with every
-- bond once and on-site weight U/2 at its two ends and U inside is a local certificate (Anderson): its translates sum
-- to (k − 1)·H, so the ground energy per site of H over all fillings is at least the least level of H_k over ALL
-- particle-number sectors, divided by k − 1. In the standard form −Σ hop + U Σ n↑n↓ at half filling the energy per site
-- is e_std = e_ph + U/4 (per site H_ph = H_std − (U/2)n + U/4, and n = 1).
-- States: a bit list of length 2k, the ↑ occupations of sites 0 … k−1, then the ↓ occupations. With the modes ordered
-- all ↑ then all ↓, a hop between neighbouring sites moves a particle between adjacent modes of one species, so no
-- fermion sign arises: every off-diagonal entry is −1 (times the scale), between states that differ exactly at two
-- adjacent positions of one half. (n↑ − ½)(n↓ − ½) is ¼ on an empty or doubly occupied site and −¼ on a singly occupied
-- one. The integer matrix is M = c·H_k with diagonal weights ae (ends) and ai (inside) times ±1 and hop −h:
-- U = 4: c = 2, ae = 1, ai = 2, h = 2; U = 8: c = 1, ae = 1, ai = 2, h = 1.
-- Sectors (N↑, N↓): spin flip maps (a, b) to (b, a), and the particle–hole map c_{iσ} → (−1)^i c†_{iσ}, under which the
-- hopping and each (n↑ − ½)(n↓ − ½) are unchanged, maps (a, b) to (k − a, k − b); so the sectors with a ≤ b and a + b ≤ k
-- cover all. Within a sector all off-diagonal entries are ≤ 0 and the matrix is unchanged by the mirror of the sites
-- and, when a = b, by the exchange of the species (permutations of the basis that preserve adjacency and the diagonal),
-- so the lowest level is that of the generalized problem on the orbit sums (G = BᵀMB, N = BᵀB), as in chem/local.cub;
-- where a sector's graph is disconnected the reduction is applied to the lowest level's positive vector on a
-- component, whose orbit sum is again a lowest vector.
import "local.cub"

